    "explanation": "Q1 and Q2 differ in two key aspects: 1) They select different columns for bond_type (T1.bond_type vs T2.bond_type), and 2) They apply different filtering conditions on atom_id. Q1 uses SUBSTR(T2.atom_id, 7, 2) = '45' (string comparison), while Q2 uses SUBSTR(T1.atom_id, 7, 2) + 0 = 45 (numeric conversion then comparison). This means Q1 looks for atom_id with '45' at positions 7-8, while Q2 converts that substring to a number and compares to 45. Additionally, they join different tables first (bond INNER JOIN connected vs connected INNER JOIN bond), but with the same join condition T1.bond_id = T2.bond_id, this doesn't affect results unless there are NULLs or duplicates, which aren't present here. The main divergence comes from the column selection mismatch and the different filtering logic.",
